	(property "PROJECT_NAME" "JY063 STIM stimulator")
	(property "RELEASE_BODY_1.0.0" "Added: Initial capture of the full Rev 1 channel (P5) from expected_netlist.csv and BOM.csv (P4): 14 sheets, 156 parts, 0 netlist differences, ERC clean.")
	(property "RELEASE_BODY_UNRELEASED" "Changed: Rev 1 cut to the analog path for bench bring-up (rev1-minimal-design-definition.md): HV input and fusing, clamp, buffer on the +/-9 V LDOs, Howland pump, DN2540 limiter, two PhotoMOS switches driven by ENABLE, TVS, current and electrode-voltage read-back for the FPGA ADC. 115 parts (was 156). FPGA connector J3 pinout: DAC_CMD, ENABLE, I_RETURN_ADC, V_ELEC_ADC, VMID_REF and grounds; no power. Rail shunts RSP/RSN 10 Ohm (current measurement; were 47 Ohm for the removed over-current trip). Descriptive net names (BLOCK_FUNCTION), values with tolerance / rating / size, every symbol and footprint in the project libraries, op amps drawn with their supply pins, power rails as power symbols, sheets left-to-right in stage order, top sheet unwired (sheet pins only). PCB: 4-layer JLCPCB JLC04161H-7628 stackup and cited HV design rules.\nAdded: Bench bias jumpers JP1/JP2 (41.2k across each half of the bias string) for +/-15..30 V bench supplies; current-loop header JP3 in the stimulating line; 29 test loops; M3 mounting holes H1-H4; read-back stage (OPA4192: x20.1 on the return shunt, VMID adder, divider buffer, VMID buffer); CHANGELOG.md; Report/.\nRemoved: Over-current sense, return-mismatch trip, trip comparators, fault latch, POR, rail monitors, enable logic, parking switch U6, threshold ladders (all stay simulated in 03_sim/rev1.py for Rev 2).")
	(property "RELEASE_DATE" "25-Oct-2026")
	(property "RELEASE_DATE_NUM" "2026-10-25")
	(property "RELEASE_TITLE_1.0.0" "1.0.0 - 2026-10-23")
